Vendor Risk Assessment Framework

This sample framework provides a structured way to identify and assess vendor risks.

Risk category	Assessment considerations
Financial	Financial stability, pricing and payment exposure
Operational	Service continuity and supplier dependency
Commercial	Contract terms, liability and termination rights
Technology	System reliability and integration requirements
Security	Access controls, security practices and incident response
Privacy	Personal data handling and international transfers
Compliance	Regulatory and contractual obligations
Concentration	Dependency on a single vendor or supplier

Suggested risk rating

* Low: Standard controls appear adequate.
* Medium: Additional review or mitigation may be required.
* High: Escalation and documented approval are required.

Risk management principles

1. Assess risks proportionately to the service and data involved.
2. Assign an accountable business owner.
3. Document findings and mitigation actions.
4. Escalate material or unfamiliar risks to the appropriate specialists.
5. Review risks periodically and when material changes occur.

Disclaimer: This is an illustrative framework, not a validated legal, security or regulatory assessment methodology.